Paralax patch for Jolt Physics v5.6.0: acquire ordering when a barrier meets a finished job.

JobSystemThreadPool queues a job created with zero dependencies at once, so a job can run to completion on a
worker before PhysicsSystem::Update adds it to the update barrier. Job::Execute publishes cBarrierDoneState with
a relaxed compare-exchange and Job::SetBarrier reads it with a relaxed compare-exchange, so in that case the
thread calling Update never synchronises with the job's writes: the barrier skips the job and Update returns
with no happens-before edge to work it relies on. ThreadSanitizer reports it (under CPU load, as a race between
the ContactRemovedCallbacks job lambda and the caller's stack reuse after Update returns); on weakly ordered
hardware it is a real missing acquire. The done state is now published with release ordering and observed
with acquire ordering.

--- a/Jolt/Core/JobSystem.h
+++ b/Jolt/Core/JobSystem.h
@@ -225,7 +225,11 @@
 		inline bool			SetBarrier(Barrier *inBarrier)
 		{
 			intptr_t barrier = 0;
-			if (mBarrier.compare_exchange_strong(barrier, reinterpret_cast<intptr_t>(inBarrier), memory_order_relaxed))
+			// Paralax patch: a job created without dependencies can run and finish before the thread that created it adds
+			// it to a barrier. Execute() publishes cBarrierDoneState with release ordering; reading it here must acquire,
+			// or that thread never synchronises with the finished job's writes (the barrier skips the job). One order for
+			// both outcomes: C++17 forbids a failure order stronger than the success order.
+			if (mBarrier.compare_exchange_strong(barrier, reinterpret_cast<intptr_t>(inBarrier), memory_order_acquire))
 				return true;
 			JPH_ASSERT(barrier == cBarrierDoneState, "A job can only belong to 1 barrier");
 			return false;
@@ -249,7 +253,7 @@
 			intptr_t barrier = mBarrier.load(memory_order_relaxed);
 			for (;;)
 			{
-				if (mBarrier.compare_exchange_weak(barrier, cBarrierDoneState, memory_order_relaxed))
+				if (mBarrier.compare_exchange_weak(barrier, cBarrierDoneState, memory_order_release, memory_order_relaxed))
 					break;
 			}
 			JPH_ASSERT(barrier != cBarrierDoneState);
